{"parentUuid":"4e3d0ff7-ba2a-4288-af7f-83ebeff04bd6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e8587740-1817-4321-bc7c-520d0eac0a5b","agentId":"a92286cd9de3a8ecc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012bDfgharksAkzwSk3YxS8v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"umr AMD userspace register debugger --waves ring dump VM fault gfx11\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ring and IB Decoding — UMR: User Mode Register Debugger documentation\",\"url\":\"https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/ring.html\"},{\"title\":\"amd/umr - AMDGPU User-Mode Register debugger\",\"url\":\"https://cgit.freedesktop.org/amd/umr/log\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction — UMR: User Mode Register Debugger documentation\",\"url\":\"https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/intro.html\"},{\"title\":\"AMDGPU DebugFS — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.kernel.org/gpu/amdgpu/debugfs.html\"},{\"title\":\"AMDGPU DebugFS — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://dri.freedesktop.org/docs/drm/gpu/amdgpu/debugfs.html\"},{\"title\":\"umr: AMDGPU Userspace Register Debugger | Man Page | Commands | umr | ManKier\",\"url\":\"https://www.mankier.com/1/umr\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - guaguagua/amd-umr: AMDGPU User-Mode Register debugger · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/guaguagua/amd-umr\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Debugging — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.kernel.org/gpu/amdgpu/debugging.html\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Debugging — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://dri.freedesktop.org/docs/drm/gpu/amdgpu/debugging.html\"},{\"title\":\"Re: [RFC PATCH 0/1] Add AMDGPU_INFO_GUILTY_APP ioctl\",\"url\":\"https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2305.0/00795.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about UMR and the features mentioned in your query:\n\n## UMR Overview\n\nUMR (User Mode Register debugger) is a debugging tool for Linux platforms that provides functionality to inspect the state of AMDGPU based devices. It is a tool to read and display, as well as write to AMDGPU device MMIO, PCIE, SMC, and DIDT registers via userspace.\n\n## Ring and Wave Functionality\n\nUMR can read the contents of the various GPU rings and for certain rings (gfx/compute/vcn/uvd/sdma) decode the packets. This includes support for GFX11 rings. Additionally, UMR can be used to query GFX/compute wave information from the hardware.\n\n## Virtual Memory and Debugging\n\nUMR supports functionality such as register reads/writes, ring decoding, virtual memory decoding and memory inspection. For VM faults specifically, there is an interface to use a reserved VMID for debugging processes which allows to associate logs, tracepoints and hardware dumps with stuff executed by specific processes.\n\nThe search results confirm that UMR is a comprehensive debugging tool capable of handling the ring dumps, wave queries, and VM fault inspection you're interested in for GFX11 AMD GPUs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"039c4ae9-79d4-4da3-9294-33c0a91f9460","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:24:30.333Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"umr AMD userspace register debugger --waves ring dump VM fault gfx11","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01SBoNUmUjTvLfeNpE5USJfM","content":[{"title":"Ring and IB Decoding — UMR: User Mode Register Debugger documentation","url":"https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/ring.html"},{"title":"amd/umr - AMDGPU User-Mode Register debugger","url":"https://cgit.freedesktop.org/amd/umr/log"},{"title":"Introduction — UMR: User Mode Register Debugger documentation","url":"https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/intro.html"},{"title":"AMDGPU DebugFS — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://docs.kernel.org/gpu/amdgpu/debugfs.html"},{"title":"AMDGPU DebugFS — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://dri.freedesktop.org/docs/drm/gpu/amdgpu/debugfs.html"},{"title":"umr: AMDGPU Userspace Register Debugger | Man Page | Commands | umr | ManKier","url":"https://www.mankier.com/1/umr"},{"title":"GitHub - guaguagua/amd-umr: AMDGPU User-Mode Register debugger · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/guaguagua/amd-umr"},{"title":"GPU Debugging — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://docs.kernel.org/gpu/amdgpu/debugging.html"},{"title":"GPU Debugging — The Linux Kernel documentation","url":"https://dri.freedesktop.org/docs/drm/gpu/amdgpu/debugging.html"},{"title":"Re: [RFC PATCH 0/1] Add AMDGPU_INFO_GUILTY_APP ioctl","url":"https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2305.0/00795.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about UMR and the features mentioned in your query:\n\n## UMR Overview\n\nUMR (User Mode Register debugger) is a debugging tool for Linux platforms that provides functionality to inspect the state of AMDGPU based devices. It is a tool to read and display, as well as write to AMDGPU device MMIO, PCIE, SMC, and DIDT registers via userspace.\n\n## Ring and Wave Functionality\n\nUMR can read the contents of the various GPU rings and for certain rings (gfx/compute/vcn/uvd/sdma) decode the packets. This includes support for GFX11 rings. Additionally, UMR can be used to query GFX/compute wave information from the hardware.\n\n## Virtual Memory and Debugging\n\nUMR supports functionality such as register reads/writes, ring decoding, virtual memory decoding and memory inspection. For VM faults specifically, there is an interface to use a reserved VMID for debugging processes which allows to associate logs, tracepoints and hardware dumps with stuff executed by specific processes.\n\nThe search results confirm that UMR is a comprehensive debugging tool capable of handling the ring dumps, wave queries, and VM fault inspection you're interested in for GFX11 AMD GPUs."],"durationSeconds":24.844333287999966,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e3d0ff7-ba2a-4288-af7f-83ebeff04bd6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c