{"parentUuid":"13e9f081-aeaa-4288-ace3-0e55599862d5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e8587740-1817-4321-bc7c-520d0eac0a5b","agentId":"a92286cd9de3a8ecc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014KMX44TjWHQu4ccupn9MyR","type":"tool_result","content":"# UMR Architecture - Limited Information Available\n\nBased on the provided documentation excerpt, I can only offer this limited response:\n\nThe page describes UMR as a tool that provides \"functionality to inspect the state of AMDGPU based devices\" through \"register reads/writes, ring decoding, virtual memory decoding and memory read/writes, register activity tracing, and IP block monitoring and logging.\"\n\nHowever, **the content does not contain details about:**\n\n- The specific architecture for GPU register access mechanisms\n- Support for custom register-access backends or alternative MMIO access methods\n- How to point the tool at devices not bound to the amdgpu kernel driver\n- The `--waves` command functionality or how wave status is retrieved\n- Relevant CLI options for register/wave/ring operations\n- Backend abstraction implementation details\n\nTo obtain this information, you would need to consult the complete UMR documentation at https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/ or the public repository at https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/tomstdenis/umr. The introduction page provided primarily describes UMR's purpose and development team rather than technical implementation details."}]},"uuid":"69c04b9a-c012-451c-90db-029909f1917d","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:25:51.426Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":2804,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# UMR Architecture - Limited Information Available\n\nBased on the provided documentation excerpt, I can only offer this limited response:\n\nThe page describes UMR as a tool that provides \"functionality to inspect the state of AMDGPU based devices\" through \"register reads/writes, ring decoding, virtual memory decoding and memory read/writes, register activity tracing, and IP block monitoring and logging.\"\n\nHowever, **the content does not contain details about:**\n\n- The specific architecture for GPU register access mechanisms\n- Support for custom register-access backends or alternative MMIO access methods\n- How to point the tool at devices not bound to the amdgpu kernel driver\n- The `--waves` command functionality or how wave status is retrieved\n- Relevant CLI options for register/wave/ring operations\n- Backend abstraction implementation details\n\nTo obtain this information, you would need to consult the complete UMR documentation at https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/ or the public repository at https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/tomstdenis/umr. The introduction page provided primarily describes UMR's purpose and development team rather than technical implementation details.","durationMs":3070,"url":"https://umr.readthedocs.io/en/main/intro.html"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"13e9f081-aeaa-4288-ace3-0e55599862d5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c69b1ea8de","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"amd-qwen-on-master","slug":"staged-whistling-hamster"}
