t the AMDGPU functions and registers you're looking for. The `wave_read_regs` function in the gfx_v11_0 driver writes to `SQ_IND_INDEX` with wave ID, register index, thread ID, and auto-increment fields, then reads from `SQ_IND_DATA` to retrieve register values.\n\nThe search results show this is part of the Linux kernel's AMDGPU driver implementation in `drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c`. This code handles GPU wave (work group) debugging and introspection by using the indirect index/data register pair (SQ_IND_INDEX and SQ_IND_DATA) to access GPU state information.\n\nThe related functions implement low-level GPU register reading for GFX11 architecture, which is essential for debugging GPU kernels and monitoring wave execution. The wave_read_regs function is used to read multiple sequential registers for a specific wave and thread combination.\n\nIf you're looking for more specific information about the other terms in your query (like WAVE_CMD_DATA, read_wave_status, SQ_CMD, halt, etc.), you may want to consult the AMDGPU documentation or the full source code from the Linux kernel repository, as the search results provided here focus primarily on the wave_read_regs implementation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2d54cc68-5b76-4b87-8556-95f95c83c0f3","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:26:13.134Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"amdgpu gfx_v11_0 wave_read_regs SQ_IND_INDEX SQ_IND_DATA WAVE_CMD_DATA read_wave_status SQ_CMD halt wave","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011gkK7Rc1eaUcRFATyNHGfs","content":[{"title":"linux/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c at master · torvalds/linux","url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c"},{"title":"linux/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c at master · torvalds/linux","url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c"},{"title":"[RFC 06/25] drm/amdgpu/gfx10.0: More compact reading of wave data","url":"http://www.mail-archive.com/amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org/msg131718.html"},{"title":"drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c - pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux - Git at Google","url":"https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/+/986d93f55bdeab1cac858d1e47b41fac10b2d7f6/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c"},{"title":"AMD GPU (Debugging with ROCGDB) - ROCm Documentation","url":"https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/ROCgdb/en/amd-staging/ROCgdb/gdb/doc/gdb/AMD-GPU.html"},{"title":"Syntax of GFX11 Instructions — LLVM 23.0.0git documentation","url":"https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPU/AMDGPUAsmGFX11.html"},{"title":"[PATCH 7/8] drm/amdgpu: rework gfx11 queue reset","url":"https://www.mail-archive.com/amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org/msg123355.html"},{"title":"User Guide for AMDGPU Backend - LLVM","url":"https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPUUsage.html"},{"title":"Syntax of gfx1011 and gfx1012 Instructions — LLVM 23.0.0git documentation","url":"https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPU/AMDGPUAsmGFX1011.html"}]},"I found relevant information about the AMDGPU functions and registers you're looking for. The `wave_read_regs` function in the gfx_v11_0 driver writes to `SQ_IND_INDEX` with wave ID, register index, thread ID, and auto-increment fields, then reads from `SQ_IND_DATA` to retrieve register values.\n\nThe search results show this is part of the Linux kernel's AMDGPU driver implementation in `drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c`. This code handles GPU wave (work group) debugging and introspection by using the indirect index/data register pair (SQ_IND_INDEX and SQ_IND_DATA) to access GPU state information.\n\nThe related functions implement low-level GPU register reading for GFX11 architecture, which is essential for debugging GPU kernels and monitoring wave execution. The wave_read_regs function is used to read multiple sequential registers for a specific wave and thread combination.\n\nIf you're looking for more specific information about the other terms in your query (like WAVE_CMD_DATA, read_wave_status, SQ_CMD, halt, etc.), you may want to consult the AMDGPU documentation or the full source code from the Linux kernel repository, as the search results provided here focus primarily on the wave_read_regs implementation."],"durationSeconds":5.845503042999655,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"83b23451-1943-46d0-92b0-f1bf06805e75","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c69b1ea8de","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"amd-qwen-on-master","slug":"staged-whistling-hamster"}
