{"parentUuid":"5f34d84c-fc7f-43f9-b4ad-6bec7c99ef79","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a92286cd9de3a8ecc","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CemEqt6DtoJASsTsuDkQn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JDE5u4xSTJAGVdL59gLsVA","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/master/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c","prompt":"Show the functions gfx_v11_0_read_wave_data, gfx_v11_0_read_wave_sgprs, gfx_v11_0_read_wave_vgprs, and wave_read_regs / wave_read_ind. Specifically: how does it program SQ_IND_INDEX (what fields: WAVE_ID, SIMD_ID, INDEX, THREAD_ID, AUTO_INCR, SE_ID) and read SQ_IND_DATA? What are the ixSQ_WAVE_* register indices read (SQ_WAVE_STATUS, SQ_WAVE_PC_LO, SQ_WAVE_PC_HI, SQ_WAVE_EXEC_LO/HI, SQ_WAVE_INST_DW0, SQ_WAVE_IB_STS)? Also show gfx_v11_0_select_me_pipe_q and how GRBM_GFX_INDEX/SE selection is done. And any use of SQ_CMD to halt waves."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2777,"cache_read_input_tokens":59986,"output_tokens":779,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2777},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":779,"cache_read_input_tokens":59986,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2777,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemEqsM52ueCNbU7ivEHF","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4e7a550-35fd-4580-9263-bfda065a09c4","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:26:23.414Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c69b1ea8de","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"amd-qwen-on-master","slug":"staged-whistling-hamster"}
{"parentUuid":"5f34d84c-fc7f-43f9-b4ad-6bec7c99ef79","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e8587740-1817-4321-bc7c-520d0eac0a5b","agentId":"a92286cd9de3a8ecc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016jfczotAsMtupzWuqrd4Rf","type":"tool_result","content":"# GFXHub Client IDs and Fault Status Decoding\n\n## Client IDs Array\n\nThe `gfxhub_client_ids` array maps client identifiers to names:\n\n```c\nstatic const char * const gfxhub_client_ids[] = {\n\t\"CB/DB\",           // Index 0\n\t\"Reserved\",        // Index 1\n\t\"GE1\",             // Index 2\n\t\"GE2\",             // Index 3\n\t\"CPF\",             // Index 4\n\t\"CPC\",             // Index 5\n\t\"CPG\",             // Index 6\n\t\"RLC\",             // Index 7\n\t\"TCP\",             // Index 8\n\t\"SQC (inst)\",      // Index 9\n\t\"SQC (data)\",      // Index 10\n\t\"SQG\",             // Index 11\n\t\"Reserved\",        // Index 12\n\t\"SDMA0\",           // Index 13\n\t\"SDMA1\",           // Index 14\n\t\"GCR\",             // Index 15\n\t\"SDMA2\",           // Index 16\n\t\"SDMA3\",           // Index 17\n};\n```\n\n**Index 8 is \"TCP\"** (Texture Cache Pipeline).\n\n## Fault Status Decoding Function\n\nThe decoding function extracts and displays multiple bitfields:\n\n```c\nstatic void\ngfxhub_v3_0_print_l2_protection_fault_status(struct amdgpu_device *adev,\n\t\t\t\t\t     uint32_t status)\n{\n\tu32 cid = REG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\t\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, CID);\n\n\tdev_err(adev->dev,\n\t\t\"GCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS:0x%08X\\n\",\n\t\tstatus);\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t Faulty UTCL2 client ID: %s (0x%x)\\n\",\n\t\tcid >= ARRAY_SIZE(gfxhub_client_ids) ? \"unknown\" : \n\t\tgfxhub_client_ids[cid], cid);\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t MORE_FAULTS: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, MORE_FAULTS));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t WALKER_ERROR: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, WALKER_ERROR));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t PERMISSION_FAULTS: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, PERMISSION_FAULTS));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t MAPPING_ERROR: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, MAPPING_ERROR));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t RW: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, RW));\n}\n```\n\nThe function decodes: client ID (CID) with name lookup, MORE_FAULTS, WALKER_ERROR, PERMISSION_FAULTS, MAPPING_ERROR, and RW (read/write access type)."}]},"uuid":"d664568d-e4fd-4e96-bb2e-094c4ac297df","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:26:25.872Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":18497,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# GFXHub Client IDs and Fault Status Decoding\n\n## Client IDs Array\n\nThe `gfxhub_client_ids` array maps client identifiers to names:\n\n```c\nstatic const char * const gfxhub_client_ids[] = {\n\t\"CB/DB\",           // Index 0\n\t\"Reserved\",        // Index 1\n\t\"GE1\",             // Index 2\n\t\"GE2\",             // Index 3\n\t\"CPF\",             // Index 4\n\t\"CPC\",             // Index 5\n\t\"CPG\",             // Index 6\n\t\"RLC\",             // Index 7\n\t\"TCP\",             // Index 8\n\t\"SQC (inst)\",      // Index 9\n\t\"SQC (data)\",      // Index 10\n\t\"SQG\",             // Index 11\n\t\"Reserved\",        // Index 12\n\t\"SDMA0\",           // Index 13\n\t\"SDMA1\",           // Index 14\n\t\"GCR\",             // Index 15\n\t\"SDMA2\",           // Index 16\n\t\"SDMA3\",           // Index 17\n};\n```\n\n**Index 8 is \"TCP\"** (Texture Cache Pipeline).\n\n## Fault Status Decoding Function\n\nThe decoding function extracts and displays multiple bitfields:\n\n```c\nstatic void\ngfxhub_v3_0_print_l2_protection_fault_status(struct amdgpu_device *adev,\n\t\t\t\t\t     uint32_t status)\n{\n\tu32 cid = REG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\t\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, CID);\n\n\tdev_err(adev->dev,\n\t\t\"GCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS:0x%08X\\n\",\n\t\tstatus);\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t Faulty UTCL2 client ID: %s (0x%x)\\n\",\n\t\tcid >= ARRAY_SIZE(gfxhub_client_ids) ? \"unknown\" : \n\t\tgfxhub_client_ids[cid], cid);\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t MORE_FAULTS: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, MORE_FAULTS));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t WALKER_ERROR: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, WALKER_ERROR));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t PERMISSION_FAULTS: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, PERMISSION_FAULTS));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t MAPPING_ERROR: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, MAPPING_ERROR));\n\tdev_err(adev->dev, \"\\t RW: 0x%lx\\n\",\n\t\tREG_GET_FIELD(status,\n\t\tGCVM_L2_PROTECTION_FAULT_STATUS, RW));\n}\n```\n\nThe function decodes: client ID (CID) with name lookup, MORE_FAULTS, WALKER_ERROR, PERMISSION_FAULTS, MAPPING_ERROR, and RW (read/write access type).","durationMs":6309,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/master/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfxhub_v3_0.c"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f34d84c-fc7f-43f9-b4ad-6bec7c99ef79","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c69b1ea8de","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"amd-qwen-on-master","slug":"staged-whistling-hamster"}
{"parentUuid":"d4e7a550-35fd-4580-9263-bfda065a09c4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e8587740-1817-4321-bc7c-520d0eac0a5b","agentId":"a92286cd9de3a8ecc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JDE5u4xSTJAGVdL59gLsVA","type":"tool_result","content":"# GFX v11.0 Wave Data Reading Functions\n\n## SQ_IND_INDEX Programming\n\nThe code programs `SQ_IND_INDEX` to select specific wave data:\n\n```c\nstatic uint32_t wave_read_ind(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t wave, uint32_t address)\n{\n\tWREG32_SOC15(GC, 0, regSQ_IND_INDEX,\n\t\t(wave << SQ_IND_INDEX__WAVE_ID__SHIFT) |\n\t\t(address << SQ_IND_INDEX__INDEX__SHIFT));\n\treturn RREG32_SOC15(GC, 0, regSQ_IND_DATA);\n}\n```\n\nFor register reads, the \"wave\" parameter maps to `WAVE_ID` and \"address\" maps to `INDEX`. The code does not explicitly set `SIMD_ID`, `THREAD_ID`, or `AUTO_INCR` fields in this function.\n\n## Wave Data Register Indices\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_read_wave_data` function reads these indices (prefixed with `ix`):\n- `SQ_WAVE_STATUS`\n- `SQ_WAVE_PC_LO` and `SQ_WAVE_PC_HI`\n- `SQ_WAVE_EXEC_LO` and `SQ_WAVE_EXEC_HI`\n- `SQ_WAVE_HW_ID1` and `SQ_WAVE_HW_ID2`\n- `SQ_WAVE_GPR_ALLOC`, `SQ_WAVE_LDS_ALLOC`, `SQ_WAVE_TRAPSTS`\n- `SQ_WAVE_IB_STS`, `SQ_WAVE_IB_STS2`, `SQ_WAVE_IB_DBG1`\n- `SQ_WAVE_M0`, `SQ_WAVE_MODE`\n\n## SGPR/VGPR Reading\n\nFor SGPRs, `wave_read_regs` uses `SQIND_WAVE_SGPRS_OFFSET`; for VGPRs, it uses `SQIND_WAVE_VGPRS_OFFSET`. The VGPR function accepts a thread parameter:\n\n```c\nwave_read_regs(adev, wave, thread, start + SQIND_WAVE_VGPRS_OFFSET, size, dst);\n```\n\n## GRBM Selection\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_select_me_pipe_q` function delegates to `soc21_grbm_select(adev, me, pipe, q, vm)`, which programs the `GRBM_GFX_INDEX` register to select specific processor units.\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_select_se_sh` function programs `GRBM_GFX_INDEX` with fields for `SE_INDEX`, `SA_INDEX`, and `INSTANCE_INDEX` to isolate shader engine selection.\n\n## Notable Absence\n\nThe provided code excerpt does not show explicit use of `SQ_CMD` for halting waves in these specific functions."}]},"uuid":"85022c8d-9828-42d2-9eb6-4995e4405237","timestamp":"2026-09-06T00:26:32.175Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":235166,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# GFX v11.0 Wave Data Reading Functions\n\n## SQ_IND_INDEX Programming\n\nThe code programs `SQ_IND_INDEX` to select specific wave data:\n\n```c\nstatic uint32_t wave_read_ind(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t wave, uint32_t address)\n{\n\tWREG32_SOC15(GC, 0, regSQ_IND_INDEX,\n\t\t(wave << SQ_IND_INDEX__WAVE_ID__SHIFT) |\n\t\t(address << SQ_IND_INDEX__INDEX__SHIFT));\n\treturn RREG32_SOC15(GC, 0, regSQ_IND_DATA);\n}\n```\n\nFor register reads, the \"wave\" parameter maps to `WAVE_ID` and \"address\" maps to `INDEX`. The code does not explicitly set `SIMD_ID`, `THREAD_ID`, or `AUTO_INCR` fields in this function.\n\n## Wave Data Register Indices\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_read_wave_data` function reads these indices (prefixed with `ix`):\n- `SQ_WAVE_STATUS`\n- `SQ_WAVE_PC_LO` and `SQ_WAVE_PC_HI`\n- `SQ_WAVE_EXEC_LO` and `SQ_WAVE_EXEC_HI`\n- `SQ_WAVE_HW_ID1` and `SQ_WAVE_HW_ID2`\n- `SQ_WAVE_GPR_ALLOC`, `SQ_WAVE_LDS_ALLOC`, `SQ_WAVE_TRAPSTS`\n- `SQ_WAVE_IB_STS`, `SQ_WAVE_IB_STS2`, `SQ_WAVE_IB_DBG1`\n- `SQ_WAVE_M0`, `SQ_WAVE_MODE`\n\n## SGPR/VGPR Reading\n\nFor SGPRs, `wave_read_regs` uses `SQIND_WAVE_SGPRS_OFFSET`; for VGPRs, it uses `SQIND_WAVE_VGPRS_OFFSET`. The VGPR function accepts a thread parameter:\n\n```c\nwave_read_regs(adev, wave, thread, start + SQIND_WAVE_VGPRS_OFFSET, size, dst);\n```\n\n## GRBM Selection\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_select_me_pipe_q` function delegates to `soc21_grbm_select(adev, me, pipe, q, vm)`, which programs the `GRBM_GFX_INDEX` register to select specific processor units.\n\nThe `gfx_v11_0_select_se_sh` function programs `GRBM_GFX_INDEX` with fields for `SE_INDEX`, `SA_INDEX`, and `INSTANCE_INDEX` to isolate shader engine selection.\n\n## Notable Absence\n\nThe provided code excerpt does not show explicit use of `SQ_CMD` for halting waves in these specific functions.","durationMs":7559,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/master/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v11_0.c"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4e7a550-35fd-4580-9263-bfda065a09c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/jacob/z/tinygrad","sessionId":"bbbf3962-a9cf-4c32-800a-58c69b1ea8de","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"amd-qwen-on-master","slug":"staged-whistling-hamster"}
